 triangle.","options":["66 cm²","132 cm²","39.3 cm²","76 cm²"],"why":"Area = ½ × base × height = ½ × 11 × 12 = 66 cm². (Don't forget the ½!)","src":"Review Q10(b), p.250","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{"O":[80,30],"S":[80,190],"P":[250,190]},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":["O","S","P"],"fill":"#FFF59D"},{"t":"ra","v":"S","a":"O","b":"P"},{"t":"len","p":["O","S"],"s":"12 cm"},{"t":"len","p":["S","P"],"s":"11 cm"},{"t":"len","p":["O","P"],"s":"16.3 cm"},{"t":"pl","p":"O","d":[-7.5,-7.1]},{"t":"pl","p":"S","d":[-11.7,18.0]},{"t":"pl","p":"P","d":[14.5,13.8]}]}},{"q":"Find the perimeter of the triangle.","options":["51 cm","53 cm","88 cm","45 cm"],"why":"Add the 3 sides: 9 + 22 + 20 = 51 cm.","src":"Review Q10(c), p.250","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{"_A":[70,120],"_B":[110,40],"_C":[290,170],"_H":[86,45]},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":["_A","_B","_C"],"fill":"#FFE0B2"},{"t":"len","p":["_A","_B"],"s":"9 cm"},{"t":"len","p":["_B","_C"],"s":"22 cm"},{"t":"len","p":["_C","_A"],"s":"20 cm"},{"t":"seg","p":["_A",[62,30]],"dash":true},{"t":"seg","p":[[62,30],"_B"],"dash":true},{"t":"txt","at":[45,80],"s":"8 cm","size":15,"bold":true,"color":"#1565c0"}]}},{"q":"Find the area of the triangle.","options":["88 cm²","176 cm²","51 cm²","98 cm²"],"why":"Area = ½ × base × height = ½ × 22 × 8 = 88 cm². (Don't forget the ½!)","src":"Review Q10(c), p.250","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{"_A":[70,120],"_B":[110,40],"_C":[290,170],"_H":[86,45]},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":["_A","_B","_C"],"fill":"#FFE0B2"},{"t":"len","p":["_A","_B"],"s":"9 cm"},{"t":"len","p":["_B","_C"],"s":"22 cm"},{"t":"len","p":["_C","_A"],"s":"20 cm"},{"t":"seg","p":["_A",[62,30]],"dash":true},{"t":"seg","p":[[62,30],"_B"],"dash":true},{"t":"txt","at":[45,80],"s":"8 cm","size":15,"bold":true,"color":"#1565c0"}]}},{"q":"Find the perimeter of the triangle.","options":["54 cm","56 cm","99 cm","48 cm"],"why":"Add the 3 sides: 23 + 20 + 11 = 54 cm.","src":"Review Q10(d), p.250","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{"_A":[40,170],"_B":[150,170],"_C":[280,40],"_P":[280,170]},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":["_A","_B","_C"],"fill":"#D1C4E9"},{"t":"seg","p":["_B","_P"],"dash":true},{"t":"seg","p":["_P","_C"],"dash":true},{"t":"ra","v":"_P","a":"_C","b":"_B"},{"t":"len","p":["_A","_B"],"s":"11 cm","off":16},{"t":"len","p":["_A","_C"],"s":"23 cm","off":-16},{"t":"len","p":["_B","_C"],"s":"20 cm","off":16},{"t":"len","p":["_P","_C"],"s":"18 cm","off":-18}]}},{"q":"Find the area of the triangle.","options":["99 cm²","198 cm²","54 cm²","109 cm²"],"why":"Area = ½ × base × height = ½ × 11 × 18 = 99 cm². (Don't forget the ½!)","src":"Review Q10(d), p.250","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{"_A":[40,170],"_B":[150,170],"_C":[280,40],"_P":[280,170]},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":["_A","_B","_C"],"fill":"#D1C4E9"},{"t":"seg","p":["_B","_P"],"dash":true},{"t":"seg","p":["_P","_C"],"dash":true},{"t":"ra","v":"_P","a":"_C","b":"_B"},{"t":"len","p":["_A","_B"],"s":"11 cm","off":16},{"t":"len","p":["_A","_C"],"s":"23 cm","off":-16},{"t":"len","p":["_B","_C"],"s":"20 cm","off":16},{"t":"len","p":["_P","_C"],"s":"18 cm","off":-18}]}},{"q":"Each square is 1 cm. Find the area of the shaded triangle.","options":["8.5 cm²","11.5 cm²","20 cm²","10 cm²"],"why":"Rectangle 5 × 4 = 20 cm². White triangles: 6 + 3 + 2.5 = 11.5 cm². 20 - 11.5 = 8.5 cm².","src":"Review Q11, p.250","fig":{"w":170,"h":144,"pts":{"_P":[20,124],"_Q":[98,20],"_R":[150,98]},"items":[{"t":"grid","x":20,"y":20,"cols":5,"rows":4,"size":26},{"t":"poly","p":["_P","_Q","_R"],"fill":"#BBDEFB"}]}},{"q":"The figure shows a right triangle. Find its area.","options":["33.92 cm²","67.84 cm²","17 cm²","34 cm²"],"why":"½ × 6.4 × 10.6: 6.4 × 10.6 = 67.84, and 67.84 ÷ 2 = 33.92 cm².","src":"Review Q12(a), p.251","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{"_A":[120,20],"_B":[120,200],"_C":[190,200]},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":["_A","_B","_C"],"fill":"#BBDEFB"},{"t":"ra","v":"_B","a":"_A","b":"_C"},{"t":"len","p":["_A","_B"],"s":"10.6 cm","off":22},{"t":"len","p":["_B","_C"],"s":"6.4 cm","off":16}]}},{"q":"How many of these right triangles (6.4 cm by 10.6 cm) can fit on a 32 cm by 22 cm card?","options":["20","10","40","15"],"why":"32 ÷ 6.4 = 5 rectangles across, 22 ÷ 10.6 gives 2 rows: 10 rectangles. Each holds 2 triangles: 20.","src":"Review Q12(b), p.251","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{"_A":[120,20],"_B":[120,200],"_C":[190,200]},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":["_A","_B","_C"],"fill":"#BBDEFB"},{"t":"ra","v":"_B","a":"_A","b":"_C"},{"t":"len","p":["_A","_B"],"s":"10.6 cm","off":22},{"t":"len","p":["_B","_C"],"s":"6.4 cm","off":16}]}},{"q":"Paul bent a wire into an equilateral triangle of side 24 cm. How long was the wire?","options":["72 cm","48 cm","24 cm","576 cm"],"why":"The wire goes all the way round: 24 + 24 + 24 = 72 cm.","src":"Review Q13, p.252","fig":null},{"q":"A triangular tray has height 20 cm and base 48 cm. Find its area.","options":["480 cm²","960 cm²","68 cm²","240 cm²"],"why":"½ × 48 × 20 = 24 × 20 = 480 cm².","src":"Review Q14, p.252","fig":null},{"q":"ABCD and EFGD are squares. AG = 18 cm and CE = ED. ADG is a straight line. Find the area of triangle AEG.","options":["54 cm²","108 cm²","36 cm²","162 cm²"],"why":"AG is 3 small sides, so 1 small side = 18 ÷ 3 = 6 cm. The height ED = 6 cm. Area = ½ × 18 × 6 = 54 cm².","src":"Review Q15, p.252","fig":{"w":320,"h":230,"pts":{"B":[40,30],"C":[160,30],"E":[160,110],"F":[200,110],"G":[200,150],"D":[160,150],"A":[40,150]},"items":[{"t":"poly","p":["A","B","C","D"],"fill":"#BBDEFB"},{"t":"poly","p":["E","F","G","D"],"fill":"#D1C4E9"},{"t":"poly","p":["A","E","G"],"fill":"#FFE0B2"},{"t":"tick","p":["C","E"],"n":1},{"t":"tick","p":["E","D"],"n":1},{"t":"len","p":["A","G"],"s":"18 cm","off":16},{"t":"pl","p":"B","d":[-12.7,-2.7]},{"t":"pl","p":"C","d":[4.7,-8.3]},{"t":"pl","p":"E","d":[15.5,10.9]},{"t":"pl","p":"F","d":[15.9,8.4]},{"t":"pl","p":"G","d":[12.9,16.4]},{"t":"pl","p":"D","d":[7.2,21.3]},{"t":"pl","p":"A","d":[-14.5,13.8]}]}},{"q":"A triangle has sides 28 cm, 11 cm and 22 cm. What is its perimeter?","options":["61 cm","51 cm","60 cm","71 cm"],"why":"28 + 11 + 22 = 61 cm.","src":"Exercise 1(a), p.75","fig":null},{"q":"An equilateral triangle has sides of 13 cm. What is its perimeter?","options":["39 cm","26 cm","169 cm","36 cm"],"why":"13 + 13 + 13 = 39 cm.","src":"Exercise 1(d), p.75","fig":null},{"q":"An isosceles triangle has sides 23 cm, 23 cm and 31 cm. What is its perimeter?","options":["77 cm","54 cm","85 cm","69 cm"],"why":"23 + 23 + 31 = 77 cm.","src":"Exercise 1(e), p.75","fig":null},{"q":"A triangle has perimeter 47 cm. Two sides are 15 cm and 13 cm. What is the third side?","options":["19 cm","28 cm","75 cm","21 cm"],"why":"15 + 13 = 28, and 47 - 28 = 19 cm.","src":"Exercise 3(a), p.77","fig":null},{"q":"A triangle has perimeter 52 cm. Two sides are 19 cm and 17 cm. What is the third side?","options":["16 cm","36 cm","88 cm","26 cm"],"why":"19 + 17 = 36, and 52 - 36 = 16 cm.","src":"Exercise 3(c), p.77","fig":null},{"q":"An equilateral triangle has perimeter 36 cm. How long is each side?","options":["12 cm","18 cm","108 cm","9 cm"],"why":"36 ÷ 3 = 12 cm.","src":"Exercise 3(d), p.77","fig":null},{"q":"A triangle has sides 2.5 cm, 4.1 cm and 6 cm. What is its perimeter?","options":["12.6 cm","12.5 cm","11.6 cm","13.6 cm"],"why":"2.5 + 4.1 = 6.6, and 6.6 + 6 = 12.6 cm.","src":"Exercise 2(c), p.76","fig":null},{"q":"A triangle has base 8 cm and height 6 cm. What is its area?","options":["24 cm²","48 cm²","14 cm²","28 cm²"],"why":"½ × 8 × 6 = 24 cm².","src":"Do and Learn 1, p.82","fig":null},{"q":"A right triangle has sides 5 cm, 12 cm and 13 cm. What is its area?","options":["30 cm²","60 cm²","32.5 cm²","78 cm²"],"why":"Use the 2 sides at the right angle: ½ × 5 × 12 = 30 cm².","src":"Do and Learn 2(b), p.82","fig":null},{"q":"A triangle has base 20 cm and height 26 cm. What is its area?","options":["260 cm²","520 cm²","46 cm²","280 cm²"],"why":"½ × 20 × 26 = 10 × 26 = 260 cm².","src":"Exercise 3(a), p.86","fig":null},{"q":"A triangle has base 7 cm and height 24 cm. What is its area?","options":["84 cm²","168 cm²","31 cm²","87.5 cm²"],"why":"½ × 7 × 24 = 7 × 12 = 84 cm².","src":"Exercise 3(c), p.86","fig":null},{"q":"A triangle has base 30 m and height 15 m. What is its area?","options":["225 m²","450 m²","45 m²","225 m"],"why":"½ × 30 × 15 = 15 × 15 = 225 m². Area uses m².","src":"Exercise 3(h), p.87","fig":null},{"q":"A triangle has base 8 m and height 35 m. What is its area?","options":["140 m²","280 m²","43 m²","148 m²"],"why":"½ × 8 × 35 = 4 × 35 = 140 m².","src":"Exercise 3(e), p.87","fig":null},{"q":"ABCD is a square of side 12 cm and E is the middle of DC. Find the area of triangle AEC.","options":["36 cm²","72 cm²","144 cm²","24 cm²"],"why":"Base EC = 6 cm, height 12 cm: ½ × 6 × 12 = 36 cm².","src":"Exercise 4(a), p.88","fig":null},{"q":"Triangle ABC has area 56 cm². Triangle DBE is half of it. What is the area of DBE?","options":["28 cm²","112 cm²","56 cm²","14 cm²"],"why":"Half of 56 is 28 cm².","src":"Exercise 4(b), p.88","fig":null},{"q":"A rectangle is 5 cm by 4 cm. The white triangles inside add up to 13 cm². What is the shaded area?","options":["7 cm²","33 cm²","13 cm²","9 cm²"],"why":"5 × 4 = 20, and 20 - 13 = 7 cm².","src":"Exercise 2(a), p.84","fig":null},{"q":"An isosceles triangle has perimeter 46.5 cm. The 2 equal sides are 14.5 cm each. What is the base?","options":["17.5 cm","32 cm","29 cm","18.5 cm"],"why":"14.5 + 14.5 = 29, and 46.5 - 29 = 17.5 cm.","src":"Do and Learn 1, p.93","fig":null},{"q":"An isosceles triangle has base 36.5 cm and 2 equal sides of 22.5 cm. What is its perimeter?","options":["81.5 cm","59 cm","82.5 cm","95.5 cm"],"why":"36.5 + 22.5 + 22.5 = 81.5 cm.","src":"Exercise 1, p.94","fig":null},{"q":"An equilateral playground has sides of 15.5 m. What is its perimeter?","options":["46.5 m","31 m","45.5 m","46.5 m²"],"why":"15.5 + 15.5 + 15.5 = 46.5 m.","src":"Exercise 3, p.95","fig":null},{"q":"An isosceles field has perimeter 96 m. The different side is 34 m. How long is each equal side?","options":["31 m","62 m","65 m","48 m"],"why":"96 - 34 = 62, and 62 ÷ 2 = 31 m.","src":"Exercise 4, p.95","fig":null},{"q":"Part B is a triangle with base 37 m and height 24 m. What is its area?","options":["444 m²","888 m²","61 m²","456 m²"],"why":"½ × 37 × 24 = 37 × 12 = 444 m².","src":"Exercise 5, p.96","fig":null},{"q":"A rectangle has area 80 cm² and length 10 cm. What is its width?","options":["8 cm","70 cm","800 cm","4 cm"],"why":"80 ÷ 10 = 8 cm.","src":"Exercise 7, p.97","fig":null},{"q":"A scarf has sides 1.2 m, 0.8 m and 0.8 m. What is its perimeter in cm?","options":["280 cm","2.8 cm","28 cm","200 cm"],"why":"1.2 + 0.8 + 0.8 = 2.8 m, and 2.8 × 100 = 280 cm.","src":"p.91","fig":null},{"q":"A big square has area 64 cm². ¼ of it is covered. What area is covered?","options":["16 cm²","32 cm²","256 cm²","8 cm²"],"why":"64 ÷ 4 = 16 cm².","src":"Let's Think Along, p.99","fig":null},{"q":"A big square has area 100 cm². How long is each side?","options":["10 cm","25 cm","50 cm","100 cm"],"why":"10 × 10 = 100, so each side is 10 cm.","src":"Problem Solving, p.101","fig":null},{"q":"4 right triangles, each with base 6 cm and height 8 cm, have a total area of…","options":["96 cm²","24 cm²","192 cm²","48 cm²"],"why":"One triangle: ½ × 6 × 8 = 24 cm². Four: 4 × 24 = 96 cm².","src":"Problem Solving, p.101","fig":null}]}